    "body": "### Describe the bug\n\nWith cython 3.3.0 and https://github.com/cython/cython/commit/0a948c7d65f91690674db4c855dadce501a3181d backported, the generated `Cython/_shared.c` when building itself is not reproducible.\n\nA partial diff of the generated code between two builds can be seen at https://valkyrie.yocto.io/pub/repro-fail/oe-reproducible-20261009-v2gtsbmt/packages/diff-html/7ce89b5d88a8d9664c63fe9b821b1165c15874dcb2c193cdf017450d9346e4d7.html.  My immediate hunch is that this is purely ordering related, the generated object is almost identical and the source diff appears to be simply code moving around.\n\nHowever, non-reproducible output breaks our build, and the debug sources count as output.\n\n\n### Code to reproduce the behaviour:\n\n_No response_\n\n### Expected behaviour\n\n_No response_\n\n### OS\n\nLinux\n\n### Python version\n\n3.14.7\n\n### Cython version\n\n3.3.0\n\n### Additional context\n\n_No response_",
